  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating climate-resilient transition of Burkina Faso</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Burkina Faso LEDS project is organized around five tasks that align to the five steps or stages typically involved in the LEDS process.Stage 1: Organize the LEDS Process (Project Task 1)Stage 2: Assess the Current Situation: Strategies, Policies, Practices, and Capacities (Project Task 2)Stage 3: Analyze Options: Identify and Analyze BAU and Low Emission Development Scenarios (Project Task 3)Stage 4: Prioritize Actions: Identify Policy, Financing, and Other Implementation Options and Priorities (Project Task 4)Stage 5: Prepare LEDS Roadmap, approve, and launch (Project Task 5)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the LEDS will be to enhance the Burkina Faso Government&#x2019;s ability to plan for decarbonization of its economy in the long-term by providing a framework and a pathway for a progressive revision and enhancement of targets under its NDC to reduce CO2 emissions to 2050. The overall impact of the project is that Burkina Faso will continue to take the lead in setting a pathway to a low carbon future and will be able to effectively plan to reduce its GHG emissions and contribute to the implementation of the Paris Agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
